; The SHAPE LANGUAGE — Pulse's foundation for saying what a value IS. One GADT type representation
; inside; plain combinators outside. From one declaration the framework derives: the codec
; (validating decode with path-collected errors), encode-side validation, normalizers, derived
; pretty-printing, and a neutral introspection [view] that downstream renderers ($jsonSchema in the
; collection lib, OpenAPI later, the admin UI later) consume without this lib knowing them.
; Deps: bson + bson_json/json (the extended-JSON bridge, so one shape drives BOTH BSON and JSON) —
; all pure + jsoo-safe, shared verbatim by server and browser. Methods and collections are disjoint
; consumers that WORK ON shapes; neither owns this.
;
; Split by concern so features/perf can grow without ballooning one file: shape.ml (the GADT
; representation), engine.ml (the interpreters — perf hacks land here), codec.ml (the `t` value +
; JSON), combinators.ml (the builder surface — features grow here). sift.ml is the thin facade that
; re-exports them as one flat module. WRAPPED with `(name sift)` so consumers see only `Sift` (the
; internals are private); userland says `Sift.string`.
(library
 (name sift)
 (public_name fennec.pulse.sift)
 (libraries fennec-mongo.bson fennec-mongo.bson_json fennec-mongo.json))
